## Show external-link badge on Designer entities with External-tab data

Context: Ontology Designer entity cards gave no visual cue that a class already
had a Dashboard, Dataset, Actions, or Bridges configured under its entity
panel's "External" tab. Users asked for a small icon near the entity icon
signalling this without opening the panel. Implemented via subagent-driven
development from a written spec and plan (docs/superpowers/specs and
docs/superpowers/plans, 2026-07-29). Live browser verification (web-devloop-tester)
caught and this session fixed a follow-on bug: the Designer's change-detection
fingerprint didn't consider the four External fields, so the badge only
appeared after a full page reload instead of immediately after saving.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/ontoviz/css/ontoviz-entity.css
   Add `.ovz-entity-external-badge` (dark badge, `--ovz-accent-purple` /
   `--ovz-entity-header-bg` tokens, no hardcoded hex) and `position: relative`
   on `.ovz-entity-icon` for the overlay anchor.
2. src/front/static/global/ontoviz/ontoviz.js
   `Entity.hasExternal` (default `false`); `_renderEntity` renders a
   `bi-link-45deg` badge inside `.ovz-entity-icon` when `hasExternal` is true;
   `pointer-events: none` keeps the existing icon-click-to-edit-icon behaviour
   working.
3. src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
   Compute `hasExternal = !!(cls.dashboard || cls.dataset ||
   (cls.actions || []).length || (cls.bridges || []).length)` and thread it
   into all three entity-build paths in `loadOntologyIntoDesigner` (saved
   layout + ontology merge, saved-layout-only fallback, fresh-layout
   generation). Also fix `_getOntologyVersion()`'s change-detection
   fingerprint to include the four External fields per class, so editing them
   and returning to the Design tab (no reload) now correctly refreshes the
   badge instead of requiring a full page reload.

