## Correction: move external-link badge from Business Views (OntoViz) to Designer (D3 map)

Context: the previous two entries built the external-link badge into the
OntoViz canvas, whose sidebar item is labelled "Business Views"
(`menu_config.json` item id `design`). The original request was for the
"Ontology > Designer" sidebar item (id `map`), which is a separate D3.js
force-directed graph (`ontology-map.js` / `_ontology_map.html`, heading
"Ontology Designer") with its own node rendering (SVG, not HTML/CSS cards)
and its own entity-data construction (a single `classes.map(...)` site, no
saved-layout persistence of class fields, and no change-detection fingerprint
to go stale). Reverted the OntoViz-side implementation and re-implemented the
same visual concept (small dark badge, `bi-link-45deg` glyph, top-right of the
icon, no tooltip/click handler) natively in the D3 view. Live browser
verification (web-devloop-tester) confirmed the badge now appears only on
Customer/Meter (the two classes with External-tab data) on the Designer graph,
is absent from all other nodes there, and is fully gone from Business Views.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/ontoviz/css/ontoviz-entity.css
   Removed `.ovz-entity-external-badge` and the `position: relative` added to
   `.ovz-entity-icon` for it.
2. src/front/static/global/ontoviz/ontoviz.js
   Removed `Entity.hasExternal` and the badge markup from `_renderEntity`.
3. src/front/static/global/js/ontology-design.js
   Removed `hasExternal` computation from all four entity-construction sites
   and reverted `_getOntologyVersion()`'s fingerprint to its prior form (no
   longer needed once the badge left this view).
4. tests/units/front/test_designer_external_badge.py
   Deleted (covered the removed OntoViz implementation).
5. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   Node data now computes `hasExternal` from the same class fields; nodes
   with the flag get a small `<circle>` + `<text>` (bootstrap-icons
   `\uf470` = `bi-link-45deg`) badge appended at (14, -14) relative to the
   node's icon, filtered so only matching nodes render it. Purely visual —
   `pointer-events: none`, no `<title>`, no click handler.
6. src/front/static/ontology/css/ontology-map.css
   `.map-node-external-badge-bg` / `.map-node-external-badge-icon` styles;
   also dims the badge alongside the icon/label under `.map-node.dimmed`
   (neighborhood-highlight mode).
7. tests/units/front/test_ontology_map_external_badge.py
   New contract tests: `hasExternal` computation, badge rendered only for
   matching nodes via `.filter(...)`, no tooltip/click handler in the badge
   block, `aria-hidden`/`aria-label` accessibility, and CSS presence
   including the dimmed-state rule.

