================================================================================
Approximate betweenness & closeness in the Databricks analytics job
================================================================================

Context: after the serverless graph-analytics job landed (PageRank, clustering
coefficient, connected components), betweenness and closeness were still the
only two metrics with no engine-side path — an oversized graph could get three
of the five per-node metrics and had to fall back to an entity-type filter for
the other two. Computing them exactly needs shortest paths from every node to
every other node (O(V*E)), which is not viable at the sizes the job exists for,
so they are now estimated with Brandes-Pich pivot sampling and clearly labelled
as estimates rather than presented as exact values.

The design decision that makes this trustworthy: the pivot set is an *input*,
not a hard-coded sample. Both estimators are written so that "pivots = every
node" reduces algebraically to the exact textbook definition, which means the
SQL can be checked against NetworkX for an exact match before any approximation
is involved. Verified: betweenness and closeness match nx.betweenness_centrality
and nx.closeness_centrality to 1e-9 on four graph fixtures, including a
disconnected graph and a 4-cycle where two shortest paths tie.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py
   Added a fifth stage to the generated SQL. `build_pivots` samples k nodes
   deterministically (`ORDER BY md5(n)` — md5 rather than a plain hash because
   it exists in both Spark and Postgres; ordering by the URI would sample one
   entity type on a real KG). `bfs_init`/`bfs_iteration` run a *single*
   multi-source breadth-first search in which all pivots advance together,
   carrying both distance and sigma (shortest-path counts), so the loop runs
   for the graph diameter rather than k * diameter. `delta_init`/
   `delta_iteration` implement Brandes' backward dependency accumulation.
   `build_centrality_rollups` reduces per-pivot results to one row per node.
   `write_output` gained `betweenness`/`closeness` columns and the two
   estimators; the summary gained `pivot_count` and `bfs_complete`. New
   `--pivots` / `--max-depth` arguments; new `_run_pivot_centrality` driver.
2. src/back/core/graph_analysis/models.py
   `MetricsResult` gained `approximate_metrics` and `pivot_count`, kept
   separate from `unavailable_metrics` so the UI can distinguish "sampled" from
   "not computed" — conflating them would either hide real numbers or present
   estimates as exact.
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobMetrics.py
   Read-back extended to the new columns and summary fields; top-nodes query now
   also unions the top-k by betweenness and by closeness. Job mode now reports
   nothing unavailable when pivots were sampled. Estimates are *withheld*
   (reported unavailable, not written onto nodes) when no pivots were sampled or
   when the BFS hit its depth cap, since a truncated search biases the distance
   sums — a wrong number is worse than a missing one.
4. src/back/core/graph_analysis/LakeflowRunner.py
   `submit`/`run_and_wait` pass a `pivots` job parameter.
5. resources/graph_analytics.job.yml
   New `pivots` job parameter (default 64) wired to `--pivots`.
6. src/shared/config/settings.py
   New `analytics_job_pivots` / `ONTOBRICKS_ANALYTICS_JOB_PIVOTS` (default 64),
   documented as the job's dominant cost.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py
   `build_job_metrics` passes the pivot setting through.
8. src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_analytics.html
   Approximate metrics render normally but carry a standing "Estimate" note
   stating the pivot count and warning that adjacent ranks can swap. The blue
   over-limit banner now says betweenness/closeness are estimated rather than
   unavailable. The amber (pushdown-only) banner now mentions that the
   serverless job exists and names the flag that enables it — its silence about
   that option was what made the feature undiscoverable.
9. tests/units/core/test_graph_analytics_job_sql.py
   New TestBetweennessAndClosenessParity: exact parity against NetworkX with a
   full pivot set on four fixtures; disconnected-component handling; sigma
   correctness on a 4-cycle; error decreasing as k grows (proves the n/k
   rescaling); determinism across runs; pivots=0 skipping both; depth-cap
   truncation reported. Dialect coverage extended to all new statements.
10. tests/units/core/test_job_metrics.py
   Output/summary fixtures carry the new columns; new tests for the two
   withholding paths and for estimates landing on nodes only when available.
11. docs/user-guide.md, docs/get-started.md
   Documented that job-mode betweenness/closeness are estimates, how to trade
   pivot count against cost, and that pivots >= node count makes them exact.

Note on accuracy (measured, karate club, 34 nodes): with a full pivot set both
metrics are exact. With k=8 the top betweenness node is still identified but
its value reads 0.328 vs a true 0.438, and closeness ranks n33 above n0 when
the truth is the reverse. Hence the UI wording: use these to find the leaders,
not as absolute values.

